Value Filldown ZONE (\S+)
Value Required INTERFACE (\S+)

# One record per interface of a security zone (eNSP Pro USG6306F, YunShan OS 1.25.1.1).
# A zone name starts at the line's first column; its interfaces are indented under
# "interface of the zone is (n):". A zone without interfaces gives no record.
Start
  ^\d{4}-\d\d-\d\d \d\d:\d\d:\d\d(?:\.\d+)?\s*$$
  ^${ZONE}\s*$$
  ^\s+priority is \d+\s*$$
  ^\s+interface of the zone is \(\d+\):\s*$$
  ^\s{2,}${INTERFACE}\s*$$ -> Record
  ^#\s*$$
  ^\s*$$
  ^. -> Error "unrecognized display zone line"
